{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Chart 22 — Access AND survival on one map (bivariate choropleth), Greater Melbourne. The §3 spatial synthesis: instead of asking the reader to scan the access map (chart-03) against the survival map (chart-18), both quantities are fused into a single area mark via a 3x3 bivariate colour scheme. Each SA2 is classed into access tertiles (share of venues within 400 m of a stop; cuts 88.9 / 97.8, computed over the 218 graded Melbourne SA2s) and survival tertiles (two-year licence survival; cuts 85.0 / 90.3), giving a 0-8 class. Colour carries both: cyan = high access only, magenta = high survival only, dark blue = both high, light grey = both low. If proximity drove survival, the high-access inner suburbs would crowd the dark-blue 'both high' corner. They don't — they read mostly cyan (high access, ordinary survival), the visible form of the flat-to-slightly-negative access-survival relationship (Pearson r = -0.13 across Melbourne; mean survival 86.9% in the top access tertile vs 89.3% in the bottom). Vega-Lite has no bivariate-choropleth idiom: the two tertile classes and their combined index are built in-spec by calculate transforms, and the 9-colour lookup is a hand-built ordinal scale. The companion 3x3 matrix legend (chart-22-bivariate-legend) decodes the colours. This map is a node of the §3 linked highlight: pick_22 captures a clicked SA2 and selected_sa2 (driven from the scatter chart-17, the maps, or the 'find your suburb' box) dims every other region. Survival is a licence-presence proxy; association only. Data: chart_sa2_survival.csv joined to sa2_melbourne.topojson on sa2_code_2021.",
  "title": {
    "text": "Inner Melbourne glows cyan — high access, but the survival edge isn't there",
    "subtitle": [
      "Each SA2 coloured by access (→) and two-year survival (↑) · dark blue = high on both.",
      "Cyan = access only, magenta = survival only · 224 SA2s in Greater Melbourne · correlation −0.13."
    ],
    "anchor": "start",
    "subtitleFontStyle": "italic"
  },
  "width": "container",
  "height": 460,
  "autosize": {
    "type": "fit-x",
    "contains": "padding"
  },
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "selected_sa2",
      "value": null
    }
  ],
  "projection": {
    "type": "conicEqualArea",
    "rotate": [
      -145,
      0,
      0
    ],
    "center": [
      0,
      -37
    ],
    "parallels": [
      -36,
      -38
    ]
  },
  "layer": [
    {
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "pick_22",
          "select": {
            "type": "point",
            "fields": [
              "sa2_code_2021"
            ],
            "on": "click",
            "toggle": "event.shiftKey"
          }
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "url": "data/sa2_melbourne.topojson",
        "format": {
          "type": "topojson",
          "feature": "sa2_summary"
        }
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "lookup": "properties.sa2_code_2021",
          "from": {
            "data": {
              "url": "data/chart_sa2_survival.csv",
              "format": {
                "parse": {
                  "sa2_code_2021": "string"
                }
              }
            },
            "key": "sa2_code_2021",
            "fields": [
              "survival_rate_pct",
              "share_400",
              "sa2_name_2021",
              "metro_regional_majority",
              "cohort_count",
              "median_nearest_stop_distance_m",
              "irsad_aus_decile"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "calculate": "datum.properties.sa2_code_2021",
          "as": "sa2_code_2021"
        },
        {
          "calculate": "datum.share_400 < 88.9 ? 0 : (datum.share_400 < 97.8 ? 1 : 2)",
          "as": "access_class"
        },
        {
          "calculate": "datum.survival_rate_pct < 85.0 ? 0 : (datum.survival_rate_pct < 90.3 ? 1 : 2)",
          "as": "survival_class"
        },
        {
          "calculate": "datum.cohort_count < 5 ? -1 : datum.access_class * 3 + datum.survival_class",
          "as": "biclass"
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "geoshape",
        "stroke": "#ffffff",
        "strokeWidth": 0.3
      },
      "encoding": {
        "color": {
          "field": "biclass",
          "type": "ordinal",
          "legend": null,
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              -1,
              0,
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4,
              5,
              6,
              7,
              8
            ],
            "range": [
              "#e0e0e0",
              "#e8e8e8",
              "#dfb0d6",
              "#be64ac",
              "#ace4e4",
              "#a5add3",
              "#8c62aa",
              "#5ac8c8",
              "#5698b9",
              "#3b4994"
            ]
          }
        },
        "opacity": {
          "condition": {
            "test": "selected_sa2 == null || datum.sa2_code_2021 == selected_sa2",
            "value": 1
          },
          "value": 0.25
        },
        "stroke": {
          "condition": {
            "test": "selected_sa2 != null && datum.sa2_code_2021 == selected_sa2",
            "value": "#1a1a1a"
          },
          "value": "#ffffff"
        },
        "strokeWidth": {
          "condition": {
            "test": "selected_sa2 != null && datum.sa2_code_2021 == selected_sa2",
            "value": 1.6
          },
          "value": 0.3
        },
        "tooltip": [
          {
            "field": "sa2_name_2021",
            "type": "nominal",
            "title": "SA2"
          },
          {
            "field": "metro_regional_majority",
            "type": "nominal",
            "title": "Region"
          },
          {
            "field": "share_400",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Within 400 m of a stop (%)",
            "format": ".0f"
          },
          {
            "field": "survival_rate_pct",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Survived 2 yrs (%)",
            "format": ".1f"
          },
          {
            "field": "median_nearest_stop_distance_m",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Median walk to stop (m)",
            "format": ","
          },
          {
            "field": "irsad_aus_decile",
            "type": "ordinal",
            "title": "SEIFA decile"
          },
          {
            "field": "cohort_count",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Venues (2023)",
            "format": ","
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Persuasive callout anchored over the inner-east, restating what the colour shows: the transport-rich core is not the 'both high' corner.",
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {
            "lon": 145.28,
            "lat": -37.7,
            "label": [
              "If proximity paid off, the inner",
              "suburbs would be dark blue.",
              "They're cyan: access, not survival."
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "right",
        "baseline": "top",
        "fontSize": 11,
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontWeight": "bold",
        "color": "#3b4994"
      },
      "encoding": {
        "longitude": {
          "field": "lon",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "latitude": {
          "field": "lat",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "text": {
          "field": "label",
          "type": "nominal"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Arrow annotation pointing at the cyan inner-Melbourne cluster — gives a skimmer the spatial pointer without requiring them to read the main callout.",
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {
            "lon": 145.08,
            "lat": -37.77,
            "label": "↙ inner suburbs: cyan here"
          }
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "left",
        "baseline": "top",
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontWeight": "bold",
        "color": "#1a1a1a"
      },
      "encoding": {
        "longitude": {
          "field": "lon",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "latitude": {
          "field": "lat",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "text": {
          "field": "label",
          "type": "nominal"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}